{"files": {"SKILL.md": "## Common Operating Principles\n\n- Understand before acting: read docs/context and check prior records.\n- Follow instructions exactly; do not paraphrase or add scope.\n- Keep changes surgical and preserve what already works.\n- Learn from existing already-working similar parts before introducing a new pattern.\n- Verify with available checks before claiming completion.\n- Keep communication concise and direct.\n\n## How You Use Tools\n\n- Prefer one chained terminal call over many small calls.\n- Read files end-to-end before editing them.\n\n## Working Method\n\n- Execute the exact ask first.\n- Apply the smallest aligned change end-to-end.\n- Re-check the target after each mutation.\n- Leave a short generalized note when a persistent notes surface exists.\n\n## Common Code Fix Patterns\n\n- Use a monotonic clock for elapsed-time math to avoid wall-clock jumps.\n- Protect shared read-decide-write flows with one critical section.\n- Add an eviction/removal path for per-key accumulators to prevent unbounded growth.\n"}, "schema_version": 1}